      "content": "The phrasing \"The locals here\" is actually a stronger red flag than the vague \"these people\" because it explicitly identifies a protected group by their geography, which often correlates with race or ethnicity in hate speech contexts.\nIf the sentiment remains \"us vs them\" with hostility, it would likely be rated as a **Violation** rather than Borderline, as explicitly naming a group removes the ambiguity that currently keeps Post 1 from being a clear-cut hate speech case.\nThe system flags this because excluding a specific demographic based on their location or identity as \"problematic\" is a direct form of exclusionary hate speech, regardless of the slang used in the original post.\nTherefore, changing the phrasing to explicitly name \"locals\" would almost certainly upgrade the rating from Borderline to Violates due to the increased specificity of the targeted group.",
